Each group passes through existing file tracking once: canonical file lock, snapshots, sibling declaration notice and change recording. Check the lease while holding the lock and preserve cancellation and final write-time change detection. Record the combined diff under the first participating call, and identify that shared operation in every member result using user-visible history identifiers. Preserve original calls in history and return a result for every original call in call order; all group members report a group failure. Sibling sessions retain normal lock waiting, notifications and stale-lease failures. Do not infer arbitrary shell writes beyond declared modifies paths.

